title: 'snowbridge: Ethereum Gloas support in the beacon light client'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds Gloas (Glamsterdam) support to the Snowbridge Ethereum beacon light client. Two
    EIPs affect it independently.

    EIP-7688 turns `BeaconState` and `BeaconBlockBody` into progressive containers, so every
    generalized index moves even where the field itself is unchanged: `finalized_checkpoint.root`
    169 -> 735, `current_sync_committee` 86 -> 2945, `next_sync_committee` 87 -> 2946, and
    `block_roots` 69 -> 352. The first three are published in the light-client spec; `block_roots`
    is not, because the ancestry proof is a Snowbridge addition. A stale 69 there breaks every
    ancestry proof and `force_checkpoint` with it, so 352 is confirmed against a live Gloas
    client rather than derived alone.

    EIP-7732 removes `execution_payload` from `BeaconBlockBody`, so the body no longer commits
    to an `ExecutionPayloadHeader` and therefore no longer to a `receipts_root`. It commits only
    to an execution block hash, at gindex 2856. A Gloas execution proof now carries the canonical
    RLP of the execution header, authenticated by `keccak256(bytes) == committed hash`, and the
    `receipts_root` is read out of those authenticated bytes.

    Breaking changes in `snowbridge-beacon-primitives`:

    - `ForkVersions` gains a `gloas` field. Every runtime, mock and benchmark configuration must
      set it.
    - `VersionedExecutionPayloadHeader` gains a `Gloas(BoundedVec<u8, ConstU32<1024>>)` variant.
      It is appended, so existing SCALE encodings continue to decode.
    - `hash_tree_root()`, `receipts_root()`, `block_hash()` and `block_number()` are removed from
      `VersionedExecutionPayloadHeader`. `commitment()` replaces them, returning an opaque
      `ExecutionCommitment` that carries both the merkle leaf and the receipts root that leaf
      authenticates. The receipts root is reachable only through the consuming
      `receipts_root_once_proven()`, so it cannot be read off a proof that was never verified.

    In `snowbridge-pallet-ethereum-client`, `execution_header_gindex()` becomes
    `execution_commitment_gindex(is_gloas)` — after Gloas the commitment is a different field,
    not just a different index — and `verify_execution_proof` returns the authenticated
    `receipts_root` instead of `()`.

    A proof whose variant disagrees with the fork era of its beacon header slot is rejected, so
    a submitter cannot select their own verification path. The Gloas fork version and epoch are
    placeholders until the fork is scheduled; until then no epoch selects Gloas and Gloas proofs
    are refused rather than mis-verified.

    Not included: weights are still measured on pre-Gloas inputs and must be regenerated before
    this is relied on in production, and the relayer-side changes are separate.
crates:
- name: snowbridge-beacon-primitives
  bump: major
- name: snowbridge-pallet-ethereum-client
  bump: major
- name: snowbridge-pallet-inbound-queue
  bump: none
- name: snowbridge-pallet-inbound-queue-v2
  bump: none
- name: bridge-hub-rococo-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: bridge-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
